0,Huba language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huba_language,"Afro-Asiatic. Chadic. Biu–Mandara.The Huba language (Nya Huba), also known as Kilba, is a Chadic language of Nigeria.",Nya Huba,Afro-Asiatic
1,Nya Huba Language (HBB) – L1 & L2 Speakers... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/hbb/,"Nya Huba is a stable indigenous language of Nigeria. It belongs to the Afro-Asiatic language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community.",Nya Huba,Afro-Asiatic
2,Nya Huba - hbb (Afro-Asiatic) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/hbb/,"Nya Huba – hbb is in the Afro-Asiatic family, included in Afro-Asiatic, Chadic, Biu-Mandara, A, A.2, 2 language class.People Groups who primarily speak Nya Huba. To download a comprehensive people group list in spreadsheet form, visit our Research Data page.",Nya Huba,Afro-Asiatic
3,Nya Huba | Accent Network,https://accentnetwork.com/nya-huba/,"Afro-Asiatic. Nya Huba, Nigeria.Nya Huba typically follows a subject-verb-object (SVO) structure, similar to English. It has a system of noun classes that affect verb conjugation and agreement. Tense, aspect, and mood are expressed through auxiliary verbs and verb suffixes.",Nya Huba,Afro-Asiatic
